  "solution": {
    "text": "(i) Aromatic compounds having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> group can decolourise bromine water.<br />(ii) Since the compound is insoluble in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>, it shows that the compound is acidic.<br />(iii) As the compound is soluble in NaOH, this again shows that the compound is acidic.<br />The above three conclusions indicate that the compound is aromatic having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> group and acidic.<br />Hence, the answer is a phenol as it is aromatic and slightly acidic.<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0136_9ecd0eae3b1a.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 179px;\" />"
